[B]icy[cles] are[ permitted users] of the[ roadway.] The coroner did not provide any insights as[ to] why the[ driver] of the vehicle didn't see the[ bicycle] at all until impact and from the quotes it appears that[ the] coroner does not[ place] any blame[ on the motorist]. Motor[ists] have a duty to keep a proper[ lookout] and to travel at a speed that allows them to slow[ or] stop to avoid a collision[.] That did not happen in this instance[.] This sounds like an extremely sad and unfortunate incident for[ all] involved[.] If[ you have] any questions[ regarding] this post[ or] an issue[ involving Illinois] personal[ injury law], please contact[ Illinois] Bicycle Attorney Mike Keating at 312-208-7702 or MKeating@Ke[atingLegal].com.[ All] initial consultations are confidential and free[.]

